  "parameter_metadata": {},
  "narrative": {
    "key_bets": [
      "Shock ignition achieves target gain G ≈ 120 at 3 MJ laser energy — nearly two orders of magnitude above demonstrated NIF Q ≈ 2.5",
      "DPSSL laser driver scales ~50× from kJ-class demonstrators (LUCIA, Mercury, HALNA) to MJ-class operation at 10 Hz sustained repetition rate with ~10% wall-plug efficiency",
      "Tritium breeding ratio can be raised from demonstrated 3.57×10⁻⁴ to >1.0 at commercial IFE neutron flux to close the fuel cycle",
      "First wall material (tungsten or tantalum candidates) survives simultaneous 10 Hz pulsed neutron, X-ray, and ion loading at MW/m² over commercial lifetimes",
      "Cryogenic DT targets with 2 mm diameter and nanometer-scale surface finish can be mass-produced at 86,400/day for <$2.78/target (Goodin criterion)",
      "Direct-drive coupling efficiency (~4–5× better than indirect drive) is achievable at the illumination symmetry required for shock ignition",
      "Final optics and beam delivery hardware survive gigashot MTTF (315M shots/year) against neutron fluence and pellet debris"
    ],
    "eliminated_costs": [
      "No magnets, cryo-cooling infrastructure, or HTS supply chain — C220103 coils/magnets = $0",
      "No separate plasma heating or current drive system — C220104 zeroed (laser driver is the sole plasma excitation source)",
      "No direct energy conversion infrastructure (GenF uses thermal-only Rankine) — C220109 DEC = $0, avoiding BLF-style TRL 1–2 energy capture risk",
      "No hohlraum manufacturing cost versus indirect-drive ICF variants (direct drive ablates target capsule directly)",
      "No isotope separation infrastructure required on-site — C220112 = $0"
    ],
    "novel_costs": [
      "Target factory CAPEX (C220600 = $244M placeholder) for industrial cryogenic DT target fabrication at 86,400/day — no MFE analogue and no validated IFE cost model",
      "DPSSL laser driver (C220107 = $999M at $333/J baseline, sweep $300M–$3B) dominating CAS22 and representing 40–60% of plant capital structure",
      "Target injection and chamber removal systems (C220108 = $334M) for 10 Hz injection into a 1,000–3,000 K chamber while maintaining cryogenic integrity",
      "Final optics debris and neutron protection (grazing-incidence mirrors, debris shields, liquid films) for gigashot-scale survivability",
      "Oversized 8 m chamber radius (vs. 4 m framework default) required to keep X-ray flux below 1 J/cm² — drives blanket/shield volume scaling as R³"
    ],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "Target gain unvalidated at commercial parameters: NIF achieves Q ≈ 2.5 at 1–2 MJ indirect drive; G ≈ 120 at 3 MJ direct drive shock ignition has never been demonstrated and LPI effects (SRS, SBS, TPD) are excluded from the Ribeyre simulations",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Tritium fuel cycle cannot close: demonstrated TBR = 3.57×10⁻⁴ vs. required >1.0 (~3,000× gap); consumption >1 kg/day vs. global CANDU supply <2 kg/yr (~180× shortfall) — feasibility constraint not reflected in LCOE",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "First wall and final optics survivability at 10 Hz undemonstrated: pure tungsten shows significant lifetime reduction; gigashot MTTF (315M shots/yr) not achieved by any laser component; availability assumed at 0.75 with no empirical basis (−0.90 elasticity on LCOE)",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Laser driver CAPEX uncertainty spans $300M–$3B across $100–$1,000/J sweep; GenF/Thales have not published beamline count, architecture, or $/J cost; diodes must reach ~$0.007/W vs. current ~$0.02/W",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Li-6 enrichment supply chain gap: DEMO-scale demand >60 t/GW enriched lithium with no Western industrial capacity; Russia/China COLEX dominance; Hexium AVLIS at $12M seed only claims 3–5 yr to partial US independence",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Target manufacturing economics unconstrained: Goodin criterion requires <$2.78/target at 86,400/day; no public cost model exists and cryogenic DT targets at industrial throughput have never been demonstrated (C220600 ranges $100M–$500M+)",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Shock ignition LPI risk at igniting-spike intensity: OMEGA experiments partially de-risk hot-electron preheat (1–2.5% conversion, 35–45 keV) but only at ~10 kJ and 450 µm scale-length; convective SRS control at MJ scale requires additional validation",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Model energy balance inconsistency (F-1): costingfe reports P_fusion = 2904 MW vs. Ribeyre-derived 3600 MW (24% shortfall) and Q_sci = 139.1 vs. expected 120 — q_eng parameter mapping requires auditing, leaving only ~162 MWe margin after laser draw",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "O&M cost structure entirely absent: no IFE concept has published fixed+variable O&M breakdown; laser optics replacement rate, chamber replacement interval, and maintenance downtime all unquantified",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Thermodynamic cycle and chamber clearing strategy unspecified: steam Rankine assumed by analogy; no gas-jet, liquid wall, or magnetic divertor ash mitigation scheme published for 10 Hz operation",
        "severity": "low"
      },
      {
        "description": "Company early-stage risk: GenF founded January 2025, TARANIS in Phase 1 (modeling through 2027); no proprietary design documents disclosed and no third-party TEA or plant study exists for this specific concept",
        "severity": "medium"
      }
    ]
  },
